{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310541,"nonce":"oRHYnt7G+KxUolB0IhCj76umEYE=","title":"FIXED in commit e6d9d36. SymbolId → IrFunctionId map (stdlib_function_map) had no name-keyed safety net while its sibling ...","message":"**Status: FIXED** in commit `e6d9d36` (workflow `wdf5z299d`).\n\n\nTwo related maps with the same shape (SymbolId → IrFunctionId for cross-file calls):\n\n| Map | Name-keyed fixup |\n|---|---|\n| `import_constructor_name_map` | YES — `fixup_stale_constructor_ids` at compilation.rs:3655 (commit 1c97d05) |\n| `stdlib_function_map` | ~~NO~~ → now `fixup_stale_method_ids` (commit e6d9d36) |\n\nAfter BLADE cache restore + per-module renumber:\n- `renumber_and_push_import_mir` (compilation.rs:3739) rewrites by id_map of the CURRENTLY-renumbering module only\n- Entries in `stdlib_function_map` for OTHER modules survive with their old func_id\n- On first use of one of those stale entries: the cached IrFunctionId no longer points at the real impl\n\nThe constructor sibling map got a second-pass name-keyed safety net via `fixup_stale_constructor_ids`. The method map didn't. This commit closes that.\n\n\n`fixup_stale_method_ids` at compilation.rs:3670-3728:\n1. Snapshot `stdlib_function_name_map` (the qname → func_id map that's rebuilt fresh per cache cycle and is authoritative).\n2. Iterate `stdlib_function_map.iter_mut()`. For each (SymbolId, func_id) entry:\n   - Reverse-map the SymbolId to its qualified name via the symbol table.\n   - If found: look up the qname in `stdlib_function_name_map`; if present, overwrite the func_id.\n   - If not found: skip (the existing `fixup_stale_cross_module_refs` MIR walk picks up survivors).\n\nHook order at compilation.rs:2922-2925:\n1. `fixup_stale_cross_module_refs` (MIR walk via ext_names)\n2. `fixup_stale_constructor_ids` (constructor map by `\u003cClass\u003e.new` qname)\n3. `fixup_stale_method_ids` (method map by qname) — **NEW**\n\n\nThe `/tmp/trap_repro/repro.sh` STEP2 silent-exit AND the 8B Q4_K_M `[gen] streaming` silent EXIT=0 are unchanged by this fix. Phase 0 of `wdf5z299d` empirically refuted the original hypothesis:\n\n- User files compile via `compile_pre_parsed_file` (compilation.rs:5477) with NO BLADE cache write path. There is no `Main.mir.cache`.\n- STEP2 fn-ptr dump shows zero remaining 4000xx IrFunctionIds; all callees correctly renumber to 390xxx.\n- Trap-stub set is byte-identical between PASS and CRASH runs.\n\nSo the cascade root is **not stale CallDirect targets** at all. Three hypotheses survive (cheapest first):\n\n- **h1: stale `import_function_param_iface_names`** — renumber re-keys by id_map only at compilation.rs:3754-3761, no name-keyed safety net. Same shape as the asymmetry this commit closed; would benefit from the same fix pattern. Cheapest to verify: instrument fixup to dump `.len()` and sorted key list at end of fixup; diff STEP1 vs STEP2.\n- **h2: stale `interface_vtables`** slot from per-file `__vtable_init__` replay across cache cycles. Per-file vtable init runs at startup (per memory `bugs_trap_stub_cascade` import-cascade subtype); cross-cycle drift could leave a stale slot.\n- **h3: stale `field_index_map`** from `class_type_id` renumber across cycles. Less likely (field offsets are stable per-shape) but worth ruling out.\n\n\n- [[bugs-trap-stub-cascade]] — the user-visible cascade; this fix closes a parallel asymmetry but not the root cause\n- [[bugs-int64-multivar-stub-replace]] — established the fixup_stale_constructor_ids pattern this mirrors\n- [[bugs-forward-ref-stub-unresolved]] — earlier fixup_stale_cross_module_refs work (1c97d05)\n- Commit 214ed60 (workflow w38cm0vcw) — iface sibling maps persistence, same shape\n- Commit 5186eb8 (workflow w269anak1) — cache-key import-set hash, preventive\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_blade_method_id_drift_asymmetry` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}